\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Entropy regularization}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{entropy}
\tag{regularization}

\p{At a reached prefix #{h=(x,y_{<t})}, the policy's next-token entropy is}

##{
  H_\theta(h)
  =-\sum_{a\in\mathcal V}
       \pi_\theta(a\mid h)\log\pi_\theta(a\mid h).
}

\p{Let #{\eta_\theta} be a declared probability law on token prefixes
reached during the update. An \strong{entropy-regularized objective} adds
#{\lambda\,\mathbb E_{h\sim\eta_\theta}[H_\theta(h)]} with
#{\lambda\geq0} to a maximized policy objective. The prefix law is part of
the objective.}

\p{Section 3 of \citef{haarnoja2018soft} develops this maximum-entropy control
convention. Here it is specialized to an autoregressive policy.
It does not imply that trajectory entropy, position-marginal entropy, and
useful exploration move together.}
